## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: CLI-wrapper redundancy belongs in harness-doctor's diagnostics, not a new skill-builder rule. Compare actual added behavior before proposing deletion.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Harness-doctor retains an on-demand comparison of a candidate skill's decisions, checks, recovery, output contract, and discoverability with the CLI and project instructions.
- [ ] A known pure wrapper and an adequate skill are controls, supported by their actual bodies rather than title/command-count inference; inspect a bounded current candidate set.
- [ ] Propose deletion only for an established redundant wrapper, preserving findings and evidence limits. No title-based purge or automatic deletion.
- [ ] No new skill-builder rule, routine healthcheck, scheduled sweep, or merge-gate integration.
